    "created_at": "2025-05-06T11:11:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-06T11:11:13Z",
    "body": "Just using `<h> ` instead of `<h1>` is IMHO the most \"honest\" solution. It doesn't suggest anything that isn't really there. It just says: I have a headline here and the actual level will depend on context. It'd be necessary to work together with CSS though (sth. like h:level(1)) to allow for addressing a specific actual level. Is there any advantage of (ab)using h1?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
