    "created_at": "2025-05-06T11:37:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-06T11:37:36Z",
    "body": "There's a better backwards compatibility story. It also works with existing markup which doesn't use the currently non-existent `<h>`. Which in turn means it works with tools that convert other formats to HTML (such as markdown).\n\nI don't see how one proposal is more honest than the other.\n\n[Back in 2017 I wrote about how \"a new element will fix everything\" is a bad assumption](https://jakearchibald.com/2017/do-we-need-a-new-heading-element/).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
